            <ArticleTitle>[Traumatic duodenal hematoma (author's transl)].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>166-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Two cases of duodenal hematoma secondary to abdominal trauma in children are reported. The latent periods between trauma and the onset of symptoms were two and fifteen days. X-ray studies were conclusive for diagnosis. Pancreatic signs were mild in one case. Both cases were treated surgically, draining the fluid collection extramucosally. The authors advise surgical treatment whenever associated lesions need to be ruled out and when obstruction persists after the first days.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
